1
00:00:00,270 --> 00:00:02,200
[The characters, behaviors,
locations, organizations, professions,

2
00:00:02,220 --> 00:00:04,150
and events depicted in this series are entirely fictional

3
00:00:04,170 --> 00:00:06,100
and created for entertainment purposes only.

4
00:00:06,120 --> 00:00:08,050
No harm or illegal action is intended
to be promoted or encouraged.

5
00:00:08,070 --> 00:00:10,000
Viewer discretion is advised]

6
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:10,880
So...

7
00:00:11,220 --> 00:00:13,640
at what moment
do we start falling for someone?

8
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:15,040
When...

9
00:00:15,420 --> 00:00:16,560
the more they look at that person...

10
00:00:17,020 --> 00:00:17,880
the deeper they fall in love.

11
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:21,800
Ai, do you think
Jaab can win Jane's heart?

12
00:00:21,820 --> 00:00:23,580
About Jaab and Jane,

13
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:26,600
I don't think that's how it goes.

14
00:00:26,760 --> 00:00:28,160
Someone's picking me up.

15
00:00:28,280 --> 00:00:29,360
Whoa...

16
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:30,800
Who is it?

17
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:36,000
His name is Mon.

18
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:37,720
I've been talking to him.

19
00:01:03,520 --> 00:01:04,600
I'm sorry, Jaab.

20
00:01:04,720 --> 00:01:06,100
The elevator broke down,

21
00:01:06,120 --> 00:01:07,600
so we waited a while.

22
00:01:09,040 --> 00:01:10,200
- Hello, Mon.
- Hi.

23
00:01:11,720 --> 00:01:13,240
Text me when you're done, okay?

24
00:01:13,650 --> 00:01:15,200
If we're done around the same time,
maybe I can pick you up.

25
00:01:15,360 --> 00:01:16,650
That way, we won't have to
trouble him as well.

26
00:01:20,350 --> 00:01:21,240
Alright.

27
00:01:21,260 --> 00:01:22,760
I'll text you, okay?

28
00:01:23,960 --> 00:01:25,080
Do your best, alright?

29
00:01:30,860 --> 00:01:31,720
Excuse me.

30
00:03:50,880 --> 00:03:52,270
Did Khanoon know about this?

31
00:03:59,060 --> 00:04:00,120
So, what's the plan?

32
00:04:00,360 --> 00:04:02,560
Weren't you just happy as a clam
this morning, huh?

33
00:04:04,260 --> 00:04:05,260
Right?

34
00:04:05,550 --> 00:04:06,800
What even is going on?

35
00:04:07,950 --> 00:04:09,640
If you don't know,
then how would I?

36
00:04:12,060 --> 00:04:14,640
Shit... My heart is broken.

37
00:04:15,460 --> 00:04:16,700
Broken, my ass.

38
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:17,640
You two were never even a thing.

39
00:04:20,080 --> 00:04:20,960
Mek,

40
00:04:21,470 --> 00:04:23,350
you know that I'm a mess right now,

41
00:04:23,370 --> 00:04:25,200
and you're still rubbing salt
into the wound?

42
00:04:26,360 --> 00:04:29,000
Before you say anything,
think about how I'd feel, will you?

43
00:04:29,020 --> 00:04:30,360
Hell, right now...

44
00:04:31,260 --> 00:04:33,340
I'm feeling so fucking fragile!

45
00:04:37,560 --> 00:04:39,450
- Fuck...
- Aw, I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

46
00:04:41,360 --> 00:04:42,560
What are you gonna do?

47
00:04:43,440 --> 00:04:45,480
I'm moving on, of course.
What fucking else?

48
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:49,560
Shit. Who's texting me now?

49
00:04:52,960 --> 00:04:56,000
When are you picking me up
for tomorrow's scouting?

50
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:06,000
- Mek.
- Hm?

51
00:05:06,860 --> 00:05:09,150
I guess I'll move on around
tomorrow evening, then.

52
00:05:10,840 --> 00:05:12,120
- You dumb fuck!
- Ow!

53
00:05:12,260 --> 00:05:14,640
You think you can just schedule
when to move on?

54
00:05:14,660 --> 00:05:17,360
What? I'm not ready.
What should I do?

55
00:05:19,670 --> 00:05:20,600
Right, right.

56
00:05:20,760 --> 00:05:23,040
You're lucky that you found out this soon

57
00:05:23,280 --> 00:05:24,800
before falling even deeper in love.

58
00:05:24,970 --> 00:05:27,970
If you'd found out after you confessed,

59
00:05:28,870 --> 00:05:30,770
it'd be even harder to keep things
the way they were.

60
00:05:33,170 --> 00:05:34,170
You mean...

61
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:37,720
Jane and I can still go back to
being the same?

62
00:05:38,950 --> 00:05:40,080
That depends on you.

63
00:05:41,160 --> 00:05:42,460
If you're up for it, then yes.

64
00:05:43,440 --> 00:05:45,260
Jane hasn't changed a bit
to begin with, right?

65
00:05:48,920 --> 00:05:50,190
He hasn't changed at all.

66
00:05:51,290 --> 00:05:53,360
Chomphoo's group is looking for
a parking spot.

67
00:05:53,380 --> 00:05:56,120
Pun and Ai are making a U-turn.
They're almost here.

68
00:05:56,870 --> 00:05:58,460
Should we survey the area?

69
00:05:58,480 --> 00:06:00,760
Or should we wait for everyone?

70
00:06:02,150 --> 00:06:04,240
I'm still in love with you, Jane.

71
00:06:06,450 --> 00:06:07,060
Jaab?

72
00:06:08,670 --> 00:06:09,460
Huh?

73
00:06:09,860 --> 00:06:11,520
Jane... What were you saying?

74
00:06:11,870 --> 00:06:13,080
I said...

75
00:06:13,100 --> 00:06:16,200
should we survey the area now
or should we wait for everyone?

76
00:06:16,980 --> 00:06:18,240
Oh...

77
00:06:18,660 --> 00:06:20,360
We can wait.

78
00:06:33,060 --> 00:06:34,440
Are you sick?

79
00:06:35,050 --> 00:06:35,790
Uh...

80
00:06:39,360 --> 00:06:40,550
I'm fine, Jane.

81
00:06:40,960 --> 00:06:43,240
Maybe it's the hot weather.

82
00:06:43,660 --> 00:06:45,050
Are you sure you're fine?

83
00:06:47,460 --> 00:06:49,170
We can wait for the others.

84
00:06:53,470 --> 00:06:55,260
Last night, you said you'd head back
to your place.

85
00:06:56,180 --> 00:06:57,590
Why did you go out
drinking with friends?

86
00:06:59,210 --> 00:07:00,210
Oh...

87
00:07:00,230 --> 00:07:01,480
About that...

88
00:07:01,760 --> 00:07:02,760
Well...

89
00:07:03,170 --> 00:07:05,080
There was...

90
00:07:05,620 --> 00:07:07,260
It was an urgent meetup, Jane.

91
00:07:07,280 --> 00:07:08,970
Very last-minute.

92
00:07:12,860 --> 00:07:14,240
Hey, Khanoon.

93
00:07:14,350 --> 00:07:16,320
Who still leaves
their shutter sound on these days?

94
00:07:16,950 --> 00:07:18,200
I didn't mean to.

95
00:07:19,390 --> 00:07:20,320
Khanoon.

96
00:07:20,550 --> 00:07:21,480
What the fuck were you doing?

97
00:07:21,770 --> 00:07:22,770
What?

98
00:07:22,830 --> 00:07:23,960
I'm the DOP.

99
00:07:24,450 --> 00:07:26,240
I'm blocking the shots, Jaab.

100
00:07:26,270 --> 00:07:27,920
Whoa. This angle is...

101
00:07:29,720 --> 00:07:30,480
There.

102
00:07:31,480 --> 00:07:33,230
This angle is perfect

103
00:07:33,250 --> 00:07:34,920
for the 34th scene.

104
00:07:36,080 --> 00:07:37,120
Tell me if you disagree.

105
00:07:37,470 --> 00:07:39,040
Really?

106
00:07:39,150 --> 00:07:40,600
This isn't the time,

107
00:07:40,870 --> 00:07:41,560
alright?

108
00:07:45,480 --> 00:07:46,860
Hi, everyone.

109
00:07:46,880 --> 00:07:48,920
- Hello.
- Hi. Hello.

110
00:07:49,780 --> 00:07:51,960
Now that we're all here,
should we start?

111
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:54,970
Alright, let's go.

112
00:07:55,320 --> 00:07:55,840
Come on.

113
00:08:02,270 --> 00:08:03,120
The traffic was bad, huh?

114
00:08:03,590 --> 00:08:05,590
Yeah. It was terrible for us.

115
00:08:06,160 --> 00:08:07,770
Hey, Khanoon.
Where are you going after this?

116
00:08:07,790 --> 00:08:08,580
I don't know.

117
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:10,980
I'll finish the job and
head home quickly to see my partner.

118
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:12,480
I'm dying to see my partner.

119
00:08:25,050 --> 00:08:26,050
Watch out.

120
00:08:26,490 --> 00:08:27,320
That was close.

121
00:08:28,260 --> 00:08:31,840
I would've ended up hurt
if it wasn't for your spidey sense.

122
00:08:35,170 --> 00:08:35,520
Oh.

123
00:08:40,360 --> 00:08:41,480
Be careful, alright?

124
00:08:41,500 --> 00:08:42,270
Mm.

125
00:08:57,050 --> 00:08:58,840
Is it true? What you said?

126
00:09:01,160 --> 00:09:03,040
I wish it wasn't.

127
00:09:03,750 --> 00:09:05,600
But that night,

128
00:09:05,880 --> 00:09:07,050
I didn't drink,

129
00:09:07,070 --> 00:09:09,800
and Jane wasn't that drunk either.

130
00:09:14,250 --> 00:09:15,250
Pun.

131
00:09:15,670 --> 00:09:17,720
Should we warn Jaab about this?

132
00:09:22,370 --> 00:09:25,800
This stuff is very private, Ai.

133
00:09:26,450 --> 00:09:29,000
If it turned out that those two
already knew,

134
00:09:29,090 --> 00:09:30,840
but decided to stay in this affair anyway,

135
00:09:31,270 --> 00:09:32,360
then outsiders like us

136
00:09:32,740 --> 00:09:34,120
shouldn't step in.

137
00:09:36,400 --> 00:09:38,960
And what if...

138
00:09:39,220 --> 00:09:40,680
Jaab didn't know?

139
00:09:41,870 --> 00:09:42,840
Fuck.

140
00:09:42,860 --> 00:09:44,240
What the hell is all this?

141
00:09:57,170 --> 00:09:58,260
This room is nice, Jaab.

142
00:09:58,280 --> 00:10:01,380
It gets a lot of natural light,
and you can see the river from here.

143
00:10:02,040 --> 00:10:03,480
Mm...

144
00:10:04,680 --> 00:10:06,600
Actually, I like it, too.

145
00:10:06,860 --> 00:10:08,560
But it might be too narrow for the lenses.

146
00:10:10,660 --> 00:10:11,880
Too narrow, you say?

147
00:10:13,840 --> 00:10:15,120
Then we need to do the blocking, huh?!

148
00:10:15,360 --> 00:10:17,520
Come on...There you go.

149
00:10:26,150 --> 00:10:27,120
Are you hurt, Jane?

150
00:10:28,180 --> 00:10:29,120
I'm fine.

151
00:10:30,160 --> 00:10:31,400
What the fuck, Khanoon?

152
00:10:31,660 --> 00:10:33,800
What? I'm blocking the shots.

153
00:10:33,990 --> 00:10:36,200
What do actors usually do in
a bedroom scene?

154
00:10:36,530 --> 00:10:38,280
They cuddle each other in bed, right?

155
00:10:40,850 --> 00:10:42,760
Alright. Now that you're both there...

156
00:10:42,780 --> 00:10:44,480
Can you play a scene

157
00:10:44,550 --> 00:10:46,560
where you two look into
each other's eyes?

158
00:10:47,670 --> 00:10:48,740
Jaab, you're the lead.

159
00:10:48,760 --> 00:10:50,440
Can you move a bit closer?

160
00:10:50,860 --> 00:10:51,860
Closer.

161
00:10:52,380 --> 00:10:54,260
Uh, and Jane...

162
00:10:54,290 --> 00:10:55,600
Move closer to the edge of the bed.

163
00:10:55,870 --> 00:10:56,870
And then...

164
00:10:57,460 --> 00:10:58,620
How about you guys nuzzle?

165
00:10:59,850 --> 00:11:01,350
Yeah, there you go.

166
00:11:01,370 --> 00:11:03,520
Okay. This looks really good.

167
00:11:03,670 --> 00:11:05,480
Now, eye contact.

168
00:11:05,500 --> 00:11:06,530
Look at each other.

169
00:11:06,550 --> 00:11:07,780
Is that necessary?

170
00:11:07,800 --> 00:11:08,840
Of course.

171
00:11:09,740 --> 00:11:12,590
Maybe get a bit closer
while looking into his eyes.

172
00:11:12,870 --> 00:11:14,900
Closer. Closer.

173
00:11:14,920 --> 00:11:16,580
Jaab, closer.

174
00:11:16,610 --> 00:11:18,750
Yeah, like that. Jane, move up.

175
00:11:18,780 --> 00:11:19,440
There you go.

176
00:11:19,980 --> 00:11:21,200
Yeah, perfect.

177
00:11:21,220 --> 00:11:22,780
Alright. Whoa, beautiful.

178
00:11:37,470 --> 00:11:39,080
I think this works...

179
00:11:39,270 --> 00:11:41,800
Let me check on the other scenes.

180
00:11:41,980 --> 00:11:43,280
What? We're not done yet.

181
00:11:44,160 --> 00:11:44,960
Hey.

182
00:11:46,160 --> 00:11:47,160
Where are you going?

183
00:11:49,570 --> 00:11:51,240
I'll go with Jaab, okay?

184
00:11:51,550 --> 00:11:54,600
Let Pun and Ai
do the blocking shots instead.

185
00:11:55,050 --> 00:11:56,360
Alright. Sure, Jane.

186
00:12:01,590 --> 00:12:03,270
Why are you two just standing there?

187
00:12:03,290 --> 00:12:04,100
Come here.

188
00:12:04,120 --> 00:12:05,270
You always sleep at the office.

189
00:12:05,290 --> 00:12:07,060
You, on the bed.
And you, get on top of him.

190
00:12:07,080 --> 00:12:08,330
Alright. Good.

191
00:12:08,350 --> 00:12:09,320
Look at each other, okay?

192
00:12:09,400 --> 00:12:10,840
At the office, you're always looking
at each other.

193
00:12:10,860 --> 00:12:12,290
Don't get flustered now.

194
00:12:12,310 --> 00:12:13,530
Lower... That's right.

195
00:12:13,550 --> 00:12:14,260
Closer.

196
00:12:14,280 --> 00:12:16,040
Move up. You're now the lead.

197
00:12:16,060 --> 00:12:17,140
Closer. Closer.

198
00:12:17,160 --> 00:12:18,240
- Even closer?
- Yeah, closer.

199
00:12:18,430 --> 00:12:19,060
Closer.

200
00:12:19,080 --> 00:12:20,590
I said closer.

201
00:12:20,610 --> 00:12:21,740
There. Amazing.

202
00:12:21,760 --> 00:12:22,720
Now, look into each other's eyes.

203
00:12:22,880 --> 00:12:24,390
Yeah, stay close. Well done.

204
00:12:24,410 --> 00:12:26,530
You never get flustered at the office,
why are you blushing now?

205
00:12:26,550 --> 00:12:28,170
Do your best, okay?

206
00:12:33,900 --> 00:12:34,730
Jaab.

207
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:35,920
Boo!

208
00:12:37,200 --> 00:12:38,250
Ugh. Come on, Jane.

209
00:12:38,270 --> 00:12:39,420
You weren't spooked at all?

210
00:12:45,280 --> 00:12:46,980
Jane... What are you looking at?

211
00:12:49,660 --> 00:12:50,400
Well...

212
00:12:50,680 --> 00:12:51,490
Uh...

213
00:12:54,560 --> 00:12:56,280
Behind you, Jaab.

214
00:12:56,610 --> 00:12:58,040
What? What's behind me?

215
00:13:05,900 --> 00:13:06,380
Boo!

216
00:13:08,370 --> 00:13:09,800
Come on, Jane!

217
00:13:09,820 --> 00:13:11,200
You scared me.

218
00:13:14,560 --> 00:13:17,260
I guess a cutie is always a meanie, huh?

219
00:13:18,780 --> 00:13:21,040
What's wrong? Why did you left?

220
00:13:22,080 --> 00:13:23,000
It's nothing.

221
00:13:23,020 --> 00:13:24,820
Well... I'm checking on the set
for the next scene.

222
00:13:24,840 --> 00:13:27,080
I want Khanoon to shoot here.

223
00:13:28,670 --> 00:13:29,090
Mm.

224
00:13:29,110 --> 00:13:30,880
Are you sure that you're fine?

225
00:13:31,470 --> 00:13:32,240
Mm.

226
00:13:32,870 --> 00:13:33,600
Right.

227
00:13:33,970 --> 00:13:36,520
I'll get the others, then.

228
00:13:36,960 --> 00:13:37,680
Okay.

229
00:13:39,480 --> 00:13:40,560
- Boo!
- Whoa!

230
00:13:48,650 --> 00:13:51,400
Jane and I can still go back to
being the same?

231
00:13:51,760 --> 00:13:52,860
That depends on you.

232
00:13:53,640 --> 00:13:55,000
If you're up for it, then yes.

233
00:13:56,560 --> 00:13:58,440
Jane hasn't changed a bit
to begin with, right?

234
00:14:00,260 --> 00:14:01,460
Shit...

235
00:14:01,970 --> 00:14:02,840
Mek.

236
00:14:03,370 --> 00:14:04,750
What you said...

237
00:14:05,680 --> 00:14:08,070
feels like a wake-up call.

238
00:14:11,870 --> 00:14:13,800
What I mean is that...

239
00:14:13,860 --> 00:14:16,160
you have to take a step back, Jaab.

240
00:14:16,960 --> 00:14:18,880
Everything between you and Jane
can go back to how it was...

241
00:14:19,370 --> 00:14:20,650
as friends.

242
00:14:21,260 --> 00:14:22,260
Nothing else.

243
00:14:41,300 --> 00:14:42,350
- Sis.
- Hm?

244
00:14:42,460 --> 00:14:43,800
I think this place already
covers everything.

245
00:14:43,820 --> 00:14:44,760
There are many good spots.

246
00:14:44,890 --> 00:14:46,960
If you're okay with that,
then it's fine by me.

247
00:14:48,380 --> 00:14:50,600
Should we go with this place, then?

248
00:14:52,240 --> 00:14:54,160
Pun, inform the client for me, alright?

249
00:14:54,760 --> 00:14:55,720
Understood, Jane.

250
00:14:57,280 --> 00:14:58,960
Now that we're done here,

251
00:14:58,980 --> 00:15:00,080
should we head back?

252
00:15:00,540 --> 00:15:02,200
The traffic only gets worse from here.

253
00:15:02,780 --> 00:15:03,640
Right.

254
00:15:03,670 --> 00:15:05,770
You've earned an award...

255
00:15:05,790 --> 00:15:07,160
for being the most eager person
to go home.

256
00:15:07,870 --> 00:15:08,440
What?

257
00:15:08,550 --> 00:15:09,680
Of course.

258
00:15:09,700 --> 00:15:11,540
I'm dying to go back to my partner.
Gotta go.

259
00:15:11,690 --> 00:15:13,140
- What? Aren't you coming with me?!
- Come on. Let's go.

260
00:15:13,160 --> 00:15:14,360
Right. And drop me off, too.

261
00:15:15,480 --> 00:15:16,960
How are you getting home, Ai?

262
00:15:17,360 --> 00:15:19,080
- Uh...
- I'll drop him off.

263
00:15:19,510 --> 00:15:20,640
I'll pass his place on the way home.

264
00:15:25,070 --> 00:15:26,000
Okay.

265
00:15:26,160 --> 00:15:28,800
Text us in the group chat
when you're home, alright?

266
00:15:29,440 --> 00:15:30,440
Okay.

267
00:15:31,060 --> 00:15:32,060
Bye-bye, Jane.

268
00:15:32,080 --> 00:15:32,970
Bye-bye, Jaab.

269
00:15:32,990 --> 00:15:33,800
Bye.

270
00:15:34,110 --> 00:15:35,650
Come on. I'll take you home, kiddo.

271
00:15:38,320 --> 00:15:39,200
Are you heading back now?

272
00:15:40,290 --> 00:15:40,950
Mm.

273
00:16:02,960 --> 00:16:05,280
Mon isn't even close to here yet, Jaab.

274
00:16:05,760 --> 00:16:06,640
Oh, really?

275
00:16:06,990 --> 00:16:07,920
How much longer?

276
00:16:08,580 --> 00:16:10,120
Want me to drop you off at your condo?

277
00:16:10,250 --> 00:16:12,520
Or how about a restaurant instead?

278
00:16:12,670 --> 00:16:13,670
Um...

279
00:16:14,060 --> 00:16:15,920
I'll have to wait for
quite a while, but it's fine.

280
00:16:16,470 --> 00:16:17,400
Right.

281
00:16:17,610 --> 00:16:18,600
Well, then...

282
00:16:18,820 --> 00:16:20,120
we'll wait here in the car.

283
00:16:20,690 --> 00:16:21,920
I'll wait here...

284
00:16:24,760 --> 00:16:25,640
and keep you company.

285
00:16:31,870 --> 00:16:32,840
Well...

286
00:16:33,360 --> 00:16:35,440
Is it okay for this little guy
to be idling here for a while?

287
00:16:36,680 --> 00:16:37,520
What little guy?

288
00:16:39,880 --> 00:16:41,920
Oh, you mean the car?

289
00:16:42,070 --> 00:16:42,660
Mm.

290
00:16:44,070 --> 00:16:45,960
This car has a name, actually.

291
00:16:46,650 --> 00:16:47,480
What is it?

292
00:16:47,950 --> 00:16:49,040
It's called "Thua-Dam." (Black Bean)

293
00:16:50,270 --> 00:16:51,240
Thua-Dam...

294
00:16:52,690 --> 00:16:54,160
Whose idea was it?

295
00:16:54,580 --> 00:16:55,400
Mine, actually.

296
00:16:55,860 --> 00:16:57,520
So creative, right?

297
00:17:19,470 --> 00:17:21,760
Can I wait in your room instead?

298
00:17:21,920 --> 00:17:22,440
Huh?!

299
00:17:23,560 --> 00:17:26,150
Then you'll be able to take a proper rest,

300
00:17:26,570 --> 00:17:28,720
and so will Thua-Dam.

301
00:17:30,750 --> 00:17:31,520
Oh.

302
00:17:41,970 --> 00:17:43,260
Oh, Mr. Handsome #1.

303
00:17:43,280 --> 00:17:44,560
Why are you back so soon?

304
00:17:44,880 --> 00:17:46,350
Hello, Mr. Handsome #2.

305
00:17:46,370 --> 00:17:47,800
We clocked out a bit early today.

306
00:17:48,180 --> 00:17:49,480
Okay.

307
00:17:53,670 --> 00:17:55,450
Why are you smiling, you pest?

308
00:17:57,180 --> 00:17:58,050
What do you mean...

309
00:17:58,070 --> 00:18:00,240
"Mr. Handsome #1" and
"Mr. Handsome #2"?

310
00:18:02,920 --> 00:18:04,160
They're secret codes, Jane.

311
00:18:04,480 --> 00:18:07,000
If you want to come up to my room,
you tell the security guard,

312
00:18:07,280 --> 00:18:09,860
"Hello, Mr. Handsome #2. Allow me to
go up to Mr. Handsome #1's room."

313
00:18:09,880 --> 00:18:11,520
That way, you won't need a keycard.

314
00:18:13,360 --> 00:18:15,240
What? I'm serious.

315
00:18:15,350 --> 00:18:17,750
I always tell my friends this
whenever they come over.

316
00:18:17,770 --> 00:18:19,160
I'm too lazy to come down
and get them.

317
00:18:19,890 --> 00:18:20,970
Mm...

318
00:18:21,660 --> 00:18:23,280
You're not handsome at all, though.

319
00:18:23,350 --> 00:18:24,550
What? Jane?

320
00:18:24,570 --> 00:18:26,380
You're asking for trouble, huh?

321
00:18:26,400 --> 00:18:27,590
You want trouble, right?

322
00:18:33,880 --> 00:18:34,760
This way.

323
00:19:05,670 --> 00:19:07,720
Isn't your room on the 23rd floor?

324
00:19:09,260 --> 00:19:10,120
Oh.

325
00:19:10,780 --> 00:19:11,540
Yeah.

326
00:19:11,570 --> 00:19:13,950
My room is a bit messy right now,

327
00:19:13,970 --> 00:19:17,120
so I'm taking you to the rooftop instead.

328
00:19:36,470 --> 00:19:39,400
The sunset at your house is
way more beautiful.

329
00:19:41,470 --> 00:19:43,240
It's beautiful in a different way.

330
00:19:44,170 --> 00:19:46,760
Here, I don't have to look up.

331
00:20:00,060 --> 00:20:00,800
Jaab.

332
00:20:03,300 --> 00:20:04,280
About that,

333
00:20:05,070 --> 00:20:06,400
do you still want an answer?

334
00:20:07,070 --> 00:20:07,800
Huh?

335
00:20:08,730 --> 00:20:09,800
About what?

336
00:20:11,140 --> 00:20:13,680
The chemistry between two people.

337
00:20:13,880 --> 00:20:15,240
You asked me about that.

338
00:20:15,870 --> 00:20:17,870
Oh, that...

339
00:20:22,030 --> 00:20:22,920
By the way,

340
00:20:23,070 --> 00:20:24,420
both of us...

341
00:20:24,440 --> 00:20:26,040
have so much in common, don't we?

342
00:20:26,860 --> 00:20:30,000
At a glance, it might seem like
we wouldn't get along,

343
00:20:30,450 --> 00:20:31,440
but...

344
00:20:31,670 --> 00:20:33,720
we've got so much in common.

345
00:20:34,090 --> 00:20:35,000
Both of us.

346
00:20:35,480 --> 00:20:36,270
Agreed.

347
00:20:38,570 --> 00:20:39,330
And...

348
00:20:39,960 --> 00:20:42,350
do you believe in the chemistry
between two people?

349
00:20:44,200 --> 00:20:46,200
I heard about it a lot back in classes,

350
00:20:47,460 --> 00:20:49,600
whenever I had to analyze films

351
00:20:49,620 --> 00:20:50,880
and characters.

352
00:20:51,720 --> 00:20:53,520
I didn't think too much about it, though.

353
00:20:54,980 --> 00:20:55,920
Me too.

354
00:20:56,070 --> 00:20:58,640
I heard about it a lot
when I was a student, too.

355
00:21:00,800 --> 00:21:02,060
It's probably how...

356
00:21:03,220 --> 00:21:05,560
two people get along well

357
00:21:06,240 --> 00:21:07,760
without even trying.

358
00:21:16,480 --> 00:21:17,600
Something like that?

359
00:21:20,670 --> 00:21:22,080
Like...

360
00:21:22,870 --> 00:21:24,150
Jane...

361
00:21:25,520 --> 00:21:26,760
and Mon, right?

362
00:21:31,140 --> 00:21:32,080
I don't know.

363
00:21:32,400 --> 00:21:33,080
What?

364
00:21:33,320 --> 00:21:34,550
Come on.

365
00:21:34,570 --> 00:21:36,920
Don't play it cool now.

366
00:21:36,940 --> 00:21:38,260
You agreed to date him.

367
00:21:38,280 --> 00:21:39,600
How could you not know?

368
00:21:42,760 --> 00:21:43,840
We're not dating yet.

369
00:21:44,350 --> 00:21:45,720
We're just in a talking stage.

370
00:21:48,270 --> 00:21:49,080
Really?

371
00:21:54,250 --> 00:21:56,050
What you and I have...

372
00:21:56,660 --> 00:21:59,560
I think we can call it chemistry, too.

373
00:22:01,690 --> 00:22:02,720
Well...

374
00:22:02,960 --> 00:22:04,760
From what I understand,

375
00:22:06,050 --> 00:22:07,370
it's like...

376
00:22:08,020 --> 00:22:11,360
when two people are compatible.

377
00:22:12,100 --> 00:22:13,440
You and I

378
00:22:13,660 --> 00:22:14,960
are compatible, yeah?

379
00:22:15,260 --> 00:22:16,480
Do you agree?

380
00:22:25,650 --> 00:22:27,980
For a bland person like me,

381
00:22:28,360 --> 00:22:30,560
it's hard to find someone
who's compatible.

382
00:22:31,150 --> 00:22:33,880
It has to be someone very extreme,

383
00:22:36,680 --> 00:22:38,120
like Min and you, Jaab.

384
00:22:38,140 --> 00:22:40,480
You two can be my close friends
without getting bored.

385
00:22:43,370 --> 00:22:44,920
Oh... Really?

386
00:22:45,370 --> 00:22:46,080
Mm.

387
00:22:46,310 --> 00:22:47,400
I agree with you.

388
00:22:49,520 --> 00:22:51,920
Thank you for
randomly walking into my life.

389
00:22:52,860 --> 00:22:53,640
Mm.

390
00:22:56,770 --> 00:22:58,560
Mon says he'll be here in 15 minutes.

391
00:23:01,170 --> 00:23:01,880
Right.

392
00:23:09,460 --> 00:23:10,920
You never told me

393
00:23:11,770 --> 00:23:12,860
about Mon.

394
00:23:14,350 --> 00:23:15,560
What do you mean?

395
00:23:17,050 --> 00:23:19,160
Well, Mon.

396
00:23:19,370 --> 00:23:20,920
You never brought him to me...

397
00:23:21,960 --> 00:23:23,560
so that I could check him out.

398
00:23:23,580 --> 00:23:24,840
I don't know if he's a good person,

399
00:23:24,880 --> 00:23:26,360
and I don't know how trustworthy he is.

400
00:23:28,360 --> 00:23:30,060
He hit me up on Instagram.

401
00:23:30,770 --> 00:23:32,120
We traded contact info
a long time ago.

402
00:23:32,980 --> 00:23:34,800
I tried to keep in touch,

403
00:23:36,060 --> 00:23:38,320
and we've been talking ever since.

404
00:23:40,780 --> 00:23:41,550
Really?

405
00:23:42,020 --> 00:23:42,730
Mm.

406
00:23:43,520 --> 00:23:44,320
That's nice, huh?

407
00:23:53,950 --> 00:23:56,160
Why are you upset?

408
00:23:56,540 --> 00:23:58,550
You're the first person
to hear about this, Jaab.

409
00:23:59,430 --> 00:24:00,680
Before Min, even.

410
00:24:02,400 --> 00:24:03,520
Really?

411
00:24:04,450 --> 00:24:05,520
I'm the first?

412
00:24:05,900 --> 00:24:06,640
Mm.

413
00:24:07,480 --> 00:24:10,360
You're the first person I've told this to.

414
00:24:12,650 --> 00:24:13,840
I'm glad.

415
00:24:51,080 --> 00:24:52,600
What should I do, Jane?

416
00:24:55,860 --> 00:24:57,020
I'm...

417
00:24:57,860 --> 00:24:59,480
so madly in love with you.

418
00:25:26,260 --> 00:25:27,960
We can wait until the traffic gets better

419
00:25:28,460 --> 00:25:29,920
and then we'll leave.

420
00:25:32,770 --> 00:25:34,800
I hope the traffic stays heavy
until tomorrow.

421
00:25:47,880 --> 00:25:49,360
Rate me, please.

422
00:25:51,460 --> 00:25:52,620
Rate you?

423
00:25:53,720 --> 00:25:54,840
For what?

424
00:25:58,560 --> 00:25:59,960
For our date today.

425
00:26:01,860 --> 00:26:02,760
From 1 to 10,

426
00:26:03,660 --> 00:26:04,780
how did I do?

427
00:26:13,680 --> 00:26:14,480
Eight.

428
00:26:17,260 --> 00:26:18,560
Where did the other two points go?

429
00:26:20,050 --> 00:26:22,050
The A/C at the restaurant was too cold.

430
00:26:28,260 --> 00:26:29,460
Thank you

431
00:26:30,550 --> 00:26:31,950
for rating me

432
00:26:35,070 --> 00:26:36,250
and for giving me a chance.

433
00:26:55,280 --> 00:26:56,920
Hey, Jane. Wait for me.

434
00:26:58,280 --> 00:26:59,600
Jaab, again?

435
00:27:00,770 --> 00:27:01,850
I'm sorry.

436
00:27:02,560 --> 00:27:03,670
I forgot to bring mine.

437
00:27:09,060 --> 00:27:09,920
Wait.

438
00:27:12,950 --> 00:27:15,140
I think we have to do something, Ai.

439
00:27:21,370 --> 00:27:24,000
The client approved
our storyboard and ideas.

440
00:27:24,560 --> 00:27:26,600
And there were no problems with the actors.

441
00:27:26,660 --> 00:27:28,400
I've confirmed some of them.

442
00:27:29,240 --> 00:27:30,960
I've taken care of the location as well.

443
00:27:31,160 --> 00:27:32,360
There were some issues with the lighting.

444
00:27:32,550 --> 00:27:35,200
But with a generator, I think we'll be fine.

445
00:27:37,060 --> 00:27:40,820
The client made a specific request
regarding the costumes.

446
00:27:40,840 --> 00:27:41,840
They'll rent outfits from brands.

447
00:27:42,240 --> 00:27:43,760
They'll discuss that on their own.

448
00:27:43,780 --> 00:27:46,520
Our job is to send them references.

449
00:27:46,960 --> 00:27:49,620
And for the costume team...
will they send us the costumes

450
00:27:49,640 --> 00:27:51,190
or will they come to the shoot?

451
00:27:51,210 --> 00:27:52,440
They'll send a team to the shoot.

452
00:27:52,860 --> 00:27:54,000
Okay, sure.

453
00:27:54,360 --> 00:27:55,400
Oh, Pun.

454
00:27:55,420 --> 00:27:56,640
Get the client some extra monitors, too.

455
00:27:56,780 --> 00:27:59,200
A lot of them will probably be there.
It's better to get separate rooms.

456
00:27:59,370 --> 00:28:02,560
Ai and I will take turns taking care of them,

457
00:28:03,260 --> 00:28:05,360
so that Jaab won't get distracted
while he works.

458
00:28:12,080 --> 00:28:13,870
Are you worried about him...

459
00:28:15,080 --> 00:28:15,900
or are you his boyfriend?

460
00:28:19,650 --> 00:28:20,650
Shut up!

461
00:28:20,770 --> 00:28:21,960
We're in a meeting, alright?

462
00:28:22,370 --> 00:28:23,560
What the hell is wrong with you?

463
00:28:23,680 --> 00:28:24,840
I was helping you.

464
00:28:25,200 --> 00:28:26,960
Shut your damn mouth.

465
00:28:27,860 --> 00:28:28,880
Hey! Hey! Stop!

466
00:28:28,900 --> 00:28:30,060
Help me! Anyone!

467
00:28:30,080 --> 00:28:31,630
I'm being kidnapped!

468
00:28:31,650 --> 00:28:33,460
Jaab, what the hell? Hey, Jaab!

469
00:28:33,650 --> 00:28:34,880
What are you doing?!

470
00:28:37,170 --> 00:28:38,520
I need to talk to you about something.

471
00:28:38,950 --> 00:28:39,560
Hm?

472
00:28:42,800 --> 00:28:44,320
Stop stirring the pot
when it comes to Jane and me.

473
00:28:45,060 --> 00:28:46,390
What?

474
00:28:46,410 --> 00:28:48,810
If I don't help an idiot like you,

475
00:28:48,830 --> 00:28:51,120
- when will you get to...
- Somebody has been hitting on Jane.

476
00:28:52,570 --> 00:28:53,480
Hitting on Jane?

477
00:28:53,940 --> 00:28:55,840
It's just flirting, no?
What are you afraid of?

478
00:28:56,730 --> 00:28:58,930
Well... If they're not dating yet,
then he's still single.

479
00:28:58,950 --> 00:29:00,570
And if he's still single,
then it's a fair game...

480
00:29:00,590 --> 00:29:02,520
But they've been talking to each other.

481
00:29:04,070 --> 00:29:04,960
Have they?

482
00:29:05,170 --> 00:29:06,200
Yeah!

483
00:29:07,050 --> 00:29:09,580
Let's just say we're now
on the same page.

484
00:29:10,150 --> 00:29:11,660
I don't want to
talk about this anymore.

485
00:29:15,860 --> 00:29:16,740
Khanoon...

486
00:29:17,860 --> 00:29:20,000
You know pressing my shoulders
will trigger my tears.

487
00:29:20,270 --> 00:29:22,400
So why the hell did you?!

488
00:29:25,400 --> 00:29:26,380
I'm sorry...

489
00:29:30,650 --> 00:29:31,580
It's alright, though.

490
00:29:31,970 --> 00:29:33,120
I'm okay.

491
00:29:33,160 --> 00:29:34,720
I'm trying to accept the truth.

492
00:29:35,170 --> 00:29:36,570
So please,

493
00:29:36,670 --> 00:29:37,760
from now on,

494
00:29:37,830 --> 00:29:39,160
don't bring it up again.

495
00:29:39,480 --> 00:29:40,560
Whether it's about Jane,

496
00:29:40,600 --> 00:29:41,960
or my feelings for him,

497
00:29:43,240 --> 00:29:44,920
or the guy he's been talking to...

498
00:29:45,670 --> 00:29:46,680
Don't bring up any of it!

499
00:29:52,270 --> 00:29:53,470
Jaab. Khanoon.

500
00:29:54,080 --> 00:29:55,400
Listen...

501
00:29:56,640 --> 00:29:57,740
Jane's already been talking to someone,

502
00:29:57,760 --> 00:29:59,320
so please give up.

503
00:30:01,160 --> 00:30:03,000
Oh, my God.

504
00:30:03,260 --> 00:30:04,200
Pun.

505
00:30:04,750 --> 00:30:07,480
Your timing is horrendous, brother.

506
00:30:08,280 --> 00:30:10,840
I'm sorry. I really did mean well.

507
00:30:18,040 --> 00:30:18,800
Jaab!

508
00:30:19,130 --> 00:30:20,000
Jaab...

509
00:30:21,480 --> 00:30:22,600
Jaab, please...

510
00:30:23,150 --> 00:30:24,480
Don't touch me!

511
00:30:25,580 --> 00:30:27,130
It's okay, Jaab!

512
00:30:27,150 --> 00:30:29,480
Don't hold back.
Let the tears wash it all away.

513
00:30:29,670 --> 00:30:33,440
We're here with you no matter what!

514
00:30:35,270 --> 00:30:36,520
It's better to give up now

515
00:30:36,540 --> 00:30:38,320
rather than get involved in an affair.

516
00:30:41,160 --> 00:30:42,160
Hey.

517
00:30:42,180 --> 00:30:43,960
I know that you two mean well.

518
00:30:44,260 --> 00:30:45,480
- It's okay.
- Don't worry about it.

519
00:30:45,570 --> 00:30:47,640
It's okay? Oh... It's okay? Huh?

520
00:30:48,120 --> 00:30:49,000
It's okay.

521
00:30:49,040 --> 00:30:50,860
It's okay...

522
00:30:51,830 --> 00:30:53,280
Jaab already knew about it.

523
00:30:53,650 --> 00:30:56,200
Not only wasn't what you said helping,

524
00:30:56,340 --> 00:30:58,180
but it also felt like you tore his heart out,

525
00:30:58,200 --> 00:31:00,160
threw it on the ground,
and stomp it to pieces!

526
00:31:00,360 --> 00:31:01,120
- Huh?!
- What?!

527
00:31:01,870 --> 00:31:03,540
Don't let there be a third time!

528
00:31:07,050 --> 00:31:08,680
- It's okay, Jaab...
- Hey, don't touch him there!

529
00:31:14,010 --> 00:31:14,840
Uh...

530
00:31:14,920 --> 00:31:17,060
- Jaab...
- Come here, come here.

531
00:31:28,960 --> 00:31:29,840
Damn it, Mek.

532
00:31:30,160 --> 00:31:32,560
You knew. Why didn't you tell me?

533
00:31:33,050 --> 00:31:34,440
Don't blame me.

534
00:31:34,460 --> 00:31:36,360
You two are always glued together.

535
00:31:36,670 --> 00:31:38,300
How would I know that

536
00:31:38,320 --> 00:31:39,390
Jaab didn't tell you about Jane and...

537
00:31:39,410 --> 00:31:40,040
Hey.

538
00:31:40,530 --> 00:31:41,920
That's the fourth time now, damn it.

539
00:31:42,360 --> 00:31:43,360
Shut up!

540
00:31:44,860 --> 00:31:46,540
The state of you right now... Damn...

541
00:31:47,370 --> 00:31:48,600
It's okay.

542
00:31:48,880 --> 00:31:49,880
I'm fine.

543
00:31:50,150 --> 00:31:51,320
Though I'm sad,

544
00:31:51,740 --> 00:31:53,160
at least I know that I'm still handsome.

545
00:31:53,690 --> 00:31:56,280
So don't worry about me.

546
00:31:56,850 --> 00:31:58,680
Still handsome, huh?

547
00:31:59,670 --> 00:32:02,040
You look like a wet dog,

548
00:32:02,600 --> 00:32:03,910
and you're still full of yourself?

549
00:32:03,930 --> 00:32:05,800
You're one big narcissist, you know that?

550
00:32:06,280 --> 00:32:07,540
You're no longer my friend.

551
00:32:07,560 --> 00:32:08,140
Hm?

552
00:32:09,160 --> 00:32:11,670
Khanoon, cut him some slack.

553
00:32:13,130 --> 00:32:14,000
My bad.

554
00:32:15,280 --> 00:32:16,280
And what about you?

555
00:32:16,370 --> 00:32:17,600
What brings you to my office?

556
00:32:17,720 --> 00:32:19,800
Khanoon told you the news, huh?

557
00:32:20,560 --> 00:32:21,660
Not exactly.

558
00:32:21,770 --> 00:32:23,200
- I was taking Mon to the vet.
- Ouch...

559
00:32:23,530 --> 00:32:24,320
Mek.

560
00:32:24,460 --> 00:32:26,120
Can you change the name of your dog?

561
00:32:26,140 --> 00:32:27,800
I'm begging you, please...

562
00:32:28,200 --> 00:32:29,680
Such an unpleasant name.

563
00:32:30,200 --> 00:32:32,760
Right, right. I'm here because
I was taking my dog to the vet.

564
00:32:32,960 --> 00:32:36,320
Then Khanoon called me and said
there was another puppy crying here.

565
00:32:36,520 --> 00:32:37,720
So I rushed here

566
00:32:37,800 --> 00:32:40,880
in case you die from a broken heart.
I don't wanna talk to a coffin instead.

567
00:32:42,060 --> 00:32:43,560
I won't die that easily, idiot.

568
00:32:45,880 --> 00:32:47,640
Right. By the way...

569
00:32:47,760 --> 00:32:50,280
who's the guy Jane's been talking to?
Why haven't I heard of him?

570
00:32:50,300 --> 00:32:52,160
I've never known him or anything.

571
00:32:52,570 --> 00:32:54,120
It's no surprise you haven't.

572
00:32:54,450 --> 00:32:55,720
Because Jane told me that,

573
00:32:55,970 --> 00:32:59,480
"I'm giving you the honor to be
the first person to know about this, Jaab."

574
00:32:59,750 --> 00:33:00,400
Something like that.

575
00:33:01,760 --> 00:33:03,200
Not to be rude or anything,

576
00:33:03,560 --> 00:33:05,280
but allow me to be very straight

577
00:33:05,370 --> 00:33:07,250
and very biased here,

578
00:33:08,460 --> 00:33:09,480
they've only been talking,

579
00:33:09,500 --> 00:33:11,280
they're not official yet.
You have a chance, no?

580
00:33:19,990 --> 00:33:21,080
Let me see.

581
00:33:32,720 --> 00:33:33,960
Looks aren't everything, right?

582
00:33:34,150 --> 00:33:34,770
Exactly.

583
00:33:34,800 --> 00:33:37,280
It's the future that's important.
We're all grown-ups here.

584
00:33:37,540 --> 00:33:39,440
Our friend is a director!

585
00:33:39,470 --> 00:33:40,680
But Mon is...

586
00:33:40,700 --> 00:33:44,480
The top executive of a banking app
you guys use every day.

587
00:33:44,700 --> 00:33:45,600
- Huh...
- Whoa...

588
00:33:46,070 --> 00:33:47,320
Really...?

589
00:33:47,700 --> 00:33:48,660
You heard me!

590
00:33:49,340 --> 00:33:50,160
- This is tough...
- This is sad.

591
00:33:51,760 --> 00:33:53,360
I'll lose either way.

592
00:33:53,750 --> 00:33:55,120
Wouldn't it be better...

593
00:33:55,270 --> 00:33:57,360
if I stayed like this so that
Jane would still be around?

594
00:33:57,450 --> 00:33:58,370
Hey.

595
00:33:58,390 --> 00:34:00,080
Aren't you being too harsh on yourself?

596
00:34:00,730 --> 00:34:03,240
We've been friends for ages
and you still can't see it, Khanoon?

597
00:34:04,630 --> 00:34:06,880
He's been giving himself
millions of pointless reasons.

598
00:34:09,040 --> 00:34:10,120
Because in truth...

599
00:34:10,380 --> 00:34:12,400
you're just too scared that
you'll lose Jane, right?

600
00:34:13,470 --> 00:34:15,920
"Friends don't break up."
Have you listened to that song?

601
00:34:17,680 --> 00:34:18,920
And one more thing,

602
00:34:20,070 --> 00:34:22,000
I respect Jane's decision.

603
00:34:26,570 --> 00:34:27,280
Mm.

604
00:34:27,860 --> 00:34:30,160
Then we'll respect yours.

605
00:34:30,760 --> 00:34:31,970
But if you're gonna step back,

606
00:34:31,990 --> 00:34:33,240
you have to fully commit to it, alright?

607
00:34:33,570 --> 00:34:35,840
This is coming from a friend
who's always been beside you.

608
00:34:36,750 --> 00:34:38,860
Now, judging from where you and Jane
have been standing,

609
00:34:39,270 --> 00:34:40,860
I think you have crossed the line.

610
00:34:41,980 --> 00:34:43,860
He said the same thing I did, see?

611
00:34:44,560 --> 00:34:45,800
Or does Jane...

612
00:34:45,890 --> 00:34:48,120
also see you as more than a friend,
but he just doesn't realize it?

613
00:34:48,140 --> 00:34:49,160
Is that possible?

614
00:34:49,990 --> 00:34:51,400
Believe me.

615
00:34:51,750 --> 00:34:54,440
After I was introduced to his world,

616
00:34:55,270 --> 00:34:57,200
he really does see me as his close friend!

617
00:34:57,560 --> 00:34:59,200
Nothing more than that.

618
00:34:59,460 --> 00:35:00,840
So if there was somebody
who crossed the line,

619
00:35:01,060 --> 00:35:02,120
that would be me!

620
00:35:02,270 --> 00:35:03,680
I crossed it.

621
00:35:10,360 --> 00:35:11,360
Okay.

622
00:35:14,080 --> 00:35:15,400
I'll cheer him up.

623
00:35:15,860 --> 00:35:16,960
Oh, by the way,

624
00:35:17,160 --> 00:35:18,400
when do you have to pick Mon up?

625
00:35:18,460 --> 00:35:19,550
- Hey!
- Huh?

626
00:35:19,700 --> 00:35:21,920
- This is far too many times, alright?
- Sorry, I didn't mean to. I forgot...

627
00:35:22,080 --> 00:35:23,520
Mon, my ass! Change the name now!

628
00:35:23,880 --> 00:35:26,040
Alright. I'm off to pick Mon up now.

629
00:35:26,350 --> 00:35:26,910
Hey.

630
00:35:26,930 --> 00:35:28,920
- Mek, you bastard!
- It's okay. Calm down.

631
00:35:28,950 --> 00:35:30,680
He just forgot, alright?

632
00:35:33,090 --> 00:35:35,120
Mon, your daddy's coming.

633
00:35:35,140 --> 00:35:36,570
Hey, hey! Wait, buddy.

634
00:35:36,590 --> 00:35:38,320
He's picking his dog up. His dog is sick.

635
00:35:38,860 --> 00:35:40,200
You're sick, too. Sit down.

636
00:35:42,060 --> 00:35:43,000
Here.

637
00:35:43,020 --> 00:35:45,440
Auntie Kaew wanted me to give you these.
Want some?

638
00:35:45,560 --> 00:35:46,870
Freshly prepared this morning.

639
00:35:46,890 --> 00:35:48,600
They're perfectly chilled, too.

640
00:35:49,580 --> 00:35:51,000
Whoa...

641
00:35:51,090 --> 00:35:53,400
Did they come straight from Phetchabun?

642
00:35:54,470 --> 00:35:55,400
No.

643
00:35:55,570 --> 00:35:56,180
What?

644
00:35:56,440 --> 00:35:57,920
Auntie Kaew came to my place this morning.

645
00:35:57,940 --> 00:35:59,550
So she brought me some fruits.

646
00:35:59,970 --> 00:36:02,320
My fridge is very packed right now.

647
00:36:06,560 --> 00:36:07,200
Here.

648
00:36:08,340 --> 00:36:10,760
Then we'll respect your decision, too.

649
00:36:10,960 --> 00:36:12,230
But if you have to take a step back,

650
00:36:12,250 --> 00:36:13,520
you have to fully commit to it, alright?

651
00:36:13,660 --> 00:36:15,670
Now, judging from where you and Jane
have been standing,

652
00:36:15,690 --> 00:36:17,180
I think you have crossed the line.

653
00:36:18,170 --> 00:36:20,640
Has she left yet?

654
00:36:20,960 --> 00:36:22,400
How about we ask her to dinner?

655
00:36:25,140 --> 00:36:26,400
It's probably too late now.

656
00:36:26,760 --> 00:36:28,250
She's leaving in the evening.

657
00:36:28,560 --> 00:36:30,680
She only visits my place once a week
to take care of stuff.

658
00:36:30,880 --> 00:36:31,960
Mm!

659
00:36:31,980 --> 00:36:34,160
You're like a prince.

660
00:36:36,950 --> 00:36:37,600
By the way,

661
00:36:37,840 --> 00:36:38,800
for your MV film crew,

662
00:36:38,820 --> 00:36:41,960
are there any concerns?
Or do you need anything else?

663
00:36:41,980 --> 00:36:43,790
Oh, it's all good now.

664
00:36:43,810 --> 00:36:45,840
Just getting the client separate monitors

665
00:36:45,860 --> 00:36:47,620
is already a blessing for me.

666
00:36:49,680 --> 00:36:50,460
Mm.

667
00:36:51,970 --> 00:36:52,760
Eat up.

668
00:37:21,260 --> 00:37:23,430
- It's been such a long day.
- Are you tired?

669
00:37:23,450 --> 00:37:24,830
I'm fucking exhausted. Shit.

670
00:37:24,850 --> 00:37:25,850
A little bit.

671
00:37:25,870 --> 00:37:27,480
- I'll treat myself to some good food.
- Sis...

672
00:37:27,500 --> 00:37:28,800
- Oh, Khanoon.
- Hm?

673
00:37:28,840 --> 00:37:30,700
Will you pass a BTS station on the way?
Can I join you?

674
00:37:30,720 --> 00:37:32,960
I wanna drop by a mall.
I'm out of toothpaste.

675
00:37:34,940 --> 00:37:37,750
Well... My partner is picking me up tonight.

676
00:37:37,770 --> 00:37:38,600
The car's right there.

677
00:37:38,730 --> 00:37:40,640
Oh, your partner again?

678
00:37:44,370 --> 00:37:45,480
Do you want to come with me, Jaab?

679
00:37:46,360 --> 00:37:48,080
I'll tell Mon to wait at the mall

680
00:37:48,260 --> 00:37:49,520
so he won't have to come all the way here.

681
00:37:50,730 --> 00:37:52,520
Oh... Are you sure?

682
00:37:52,760 --> 00:37:54,400
I can ask my partner to drop you off.

683
00:37:58,660 --> 00:37:59,240
Mm.

684
00:37:59,450 --> 00:38:00,170
Let's go, then.

685
00:38:00,450 --> 00:38:01,560
I'll walk with you.

686
00:38:03,950 --> 00:38:05,670
I'm off, then.

687
00:38:05,690 --> 00:38:06,720
I'm too tired. Bye-bye.

688
00:38:07,300 --> 00:38:07,800
Bye.

689
00:38:07,820 --> 00:38:08,320
See you, Sis.

690
00:38:08,340 --> 00:38:09,840
- Bye-bye, Chomphoo.
- Get home safely.

691
00:38:10,960 --> 00:38:11,760
And what about you?

692
00:38:12,440 --> 00:38:14,870
Excuse us.

693
00:38:14,890 --> 00:38:16,070
- Mm.
- Mm, see you.

694
00:38:16,090 --> 00:38:17,080
- Bye-bye, everyone.
- Bye-bye.

695
00:38:17,100 --> 00:38:17,840
Bye-bye.

696
00:38:18,340 --> 00:38:19,200
- Bye-bye.
- See you.

697
00:38:23,250 --> 00:38:23,960
What?!

698
00:38:24,550 --> 00:38:25,960
Are you sure, Jaab?

699
00:38:26,230 --> 00:38:26,880
Hm?

700
00:38:27,180 --> 00:38:27,860
You told me

701
00:38:27,880 --> 00:38:31,120
you'd step back
from the line you've crossed.

702
00:38:31,450 --> 00:38:34,470
What I'm seeing right now is
you wrapping that line around your neck.

703
00:38:34,490 --> 00:38:35,100
Huh?

704
00:38:35,850 --> 00:38:36,720
What is it, Jaab?

705
00:38:38,480 --> 00:38:39,720
Bye, Khanoon.

706
00:38:40,050 --> 00:38:41,500
Bye-bye.

707
00:38:43,360 --> 00:38:44,960
Oh... Bye-bye, Jane.

708
00:38:45,060 --> 00:38:46,850
Take care of this idiot for me.

709
00:38:47,360 --> 00:38:48,360
Knock yourself out.

710
00:38:48,860 --> 00:38:49,720
I'll get going now. See you.

711
00:38:54,780 --> 00:38:55,600
Shall we?

712
00:38:57,530 --> 00:38:58,800
Mm. Let's go.

713
00:39:04,660 --> 00:39:05,660
Yes, Mon?

714
00:39:07,340 --> 00:39:08,930
Jaab and I are on the way.

715
00:39:09,970 --> 00:39:11,680
Let's meet at the restaurant, then.

716
00:39:15,220 --> 00:39:16,780
I'll try asking him.

717
00:39:21,340 --> 00:39:22,920
Mon invites you to dinner.

718
00:39:24,950 --> 00:39:26,170
Oh, that's alright.

719
00:39:26,740 --> 00:39:29,180
I'm going to the movies after this.

720
00:39:29,200 --> 00:39:30,440
There probably isn't enough time.

721
00:39:32,560 --> 00:39:33,750
Which movie?

722
00:39:36,370 --> 00:39:37,160
Uh...

723
00:39:38,570 --> 00:39:40,480
'Doraemon the Movie.'

724
00:39:40,660 --> 00:39:43,080
Another one just came out.

725
00:39:45,670 --> 00:39:48,000
But I heard this one is sad.

726
00:39:48,720 --> 00:39:51,000
You won't cry like a baby
if you watch it alone, right?

727
00:39:52,100 --> 00:39:54,640
And is it available at 3sept?

728
00:39:55,150 --> 00:39:56,150
Do you want to go together?

729
00:39:56,360 --> 00:39:57,480
Remember our promise?

730
00:39:59,560 --> 00:40:02,050
I've already bought a ticket, Jane.

731
00:40:02,070 --> 00:40:03,440
I'm sorry.

732
00:40:06,850 --> 00:40:08,920
You really won't cry, huh?

733
00:40:09,760 --> 00:40:11,000
Come on, Jane.

734
00:40:11,020 --> 00:40:12,400
This is Jaab you're talking about.

735
00:40:12,560 --> 00:40:14,040
If Doraemon makes me cry,

736
00:40:14,160 --> 00:40:16,080
you can call me a wimp!

737
00:40:18,560 --> 00:40:19,960
Mm. Let's go.

738
00:40:20,750 --> 00:40:21,580
Whoa!

739
00:40:25,130 --> 00:40:25,760
Hey!

740
00:40:26,260 --> 00:40:27,440
You call that riding?!

741
00:40:31,040 --> 00:40:31,720
Let's go, Jane.

742
00:40:31,820 --> 00:40:33,280
I'll help you cross the road.

743
00:40:50,380 --> 00:40:51,240
Let's go, Jane.

744
00:41:26,680 --> 00:41:27,420
Hello.

745
00:41:27,440 --> 00:41:28,380
Let me take care of that.

746
00:41:30,080 --> 00:41:31,160
- Good evening.
- Good evening.

747
00:41:32,350 --> 00:41:33,960
You're not joining us, Jaab?

748
00:41:34,460 --> 00:41:35,550
Oh.

749
00:41:36,540 --> 00:41:37,880
I asked him,

750
00:41:38,150 --> 00:41:40,040
but he's already bought a movie ticket.

751
00:41:40,060 --> 00:41:42,280
I was late by a millisecond.

752
00:41:43,350 --> 00:41:44,760
A millisecond?

753
00:41:45,860 --> 00:41:46,920
Come on, Mon.

754
00:41:47,160 --> 00:41:49,140
You always laugh at whatever I say.

755
00:41:49,160 --> 00:41:51,400
I'm sorry. I still can't get used to it.

756
00:41:52,160 --> 00:41:53,080
He's used to it now, though.

757
00:41:53,660 --> 00:41:54,480
Isn't that right, Jaab?

758
00:41:55,480 --> 00:41:56,040
Yeah.

759
00:41:56,250 --> 00:41:56,850
Yes.

760
00:41:56,870 --> 00:41:59,080
Jane often says things in a weird way.

761
00:42:04,150 --> 00:42:05,070
Well...

762
00:42:05,880 --> 00:42:06,880
I'll get going now.

763
00:42:07,340 --> 00:42:08,280
Or else I'll be late.

764
00:42:10,520 --> 00:42:11,280
Mon...

765
00:42:11,960 --> 00:42:13,000
- Bye-bye.
- Goodbye.

766
00:42:18,560 --> 00:42:19,320
Shall we head inside?

767
00:42:33,250 --> 00:42:35,920
When did I wanna watch 'Doraemon the Movie'?

768
00:42:37,980 --> 00:42:39,580
Damn it, Jaab...

769
00:42:42,240 --> 00:42:43,320
Eat up,

770
00:42:43,940 --> 00:42:45,540
so you'll grow a little bigger.

771
00:42:46,970 --> 00:42:47,880
Mon.

772
00:42:48,640 --> 00:42:50,840
This is as big as I can get.

773
00:42:52,660 --> 00:42:54,040
I'm kidding.

774
00:42:54,560 --> 00:42:56,520
I still want you to eat a lot, though.

775
00:42:56,770 --> 00:42:58,840
I ordered only your favorites.

776
00:43:04,120 --> 00:43:05,930
Have some salmon.

777
00:43:07,350 --> 00:43:08,920
If Jaab were here with us,

778
00:43:09,550 --> 00:43:11,370
the plates would've already been wiped clean.

779
00:43:12,450 --> 00:43:14,680
Jaab is such a hearty eater, Mon.

780
00:43:14,800 --> 00:43:16,920
All food is afraid of him.

781
00:43:20,950 --> 00:43:22,160
Is he a funny person?

782
00:43:23,050 --> 00:43:24,050
How did you know?

783
00:43:27,160 --> 00:43:29,960
You seem happy whenever you talk about him.

784
00:43:30,820 --> 00:43:31,960
So I think...

785
00:43:32,660 --> 00:43:34,560
he probably makes you smile a lot.

786
00:43:41,830 --> 00:43:43,630
This damn movie is sadder than I thought.

787
00:43:43,650 --> 00:43:45,650
Damn it. What do I do?

788
00:43:46,150 --> 00:43:48,100
Fuck. I'm so fucking sad.

789
00:43:48,120 --> 00:43:49,200
Damn it...

790
00:43:52,770 --> 00:43:53,680
Jane?!

791
00:43:53,860 --> 00:43:55,440
What are you doing? You scared me.

792
00:43:56,240 --> 00:43:58,240
You're such a wimp, Jaab.

793
00:43:58,260 --> 00:43:58,730
What?

794
00:43:58,750 --> 00:44:00,180
Hey, hey...

795
00:44:00,210 --> 00:44:02,160
You've been sitting on that one
for two hours, huh?

796
00:44:04,150 --> 00:44:04,820
Hey, Jane!

797
00:44:04,840 --> 00:44:05,570
Wait...

798
00:44:06,400 --> 00:44:07,640
Even if a shorty like you

799
00:44:07,660 --> 00:44:08,940
runs as fast as the wind,

800
00:44:08,960 --> 00:44:10,250
you can't escape me, Jane!

801
00:44:10,270 --> 00:44:11,060
Jane!

802
00:44:19,250 --> 00:44:21,250
- Jane, mosquitoes.
- Here you go.

803
00:44:21,920 --> 00:44:23,050
- Here you go.
- Oh, thank you.

804
00:44:23,070 --> 00:44:24,200
Thank you.

805
00:44:25,600 --> 00:44:26,560
Thank you.

806
00:44:28,760 --> 00:44:29,760
Whoa, Jane.

807
00:44:29,780 --> 00:44:30,760
That looks amazing.

808
00:44:30,800 --> 00:44:32,520
- Can I have some?
- Hey!

809
00:44:34,480 --> 00:44:35,240
There.

810
00:44:38,550 --> 00:44:40,160
Why didn't you go back with Mon?

811
00:44:40,760 --> 00:44:42,160
I still wanted desserts.

812
00:44:43,260 --> 00:44:45,260
It's already late. He won't eat anymore.

813
00:44:46,450 --> 00:44:48,240
And how did you know that
I'm still around?

814
00:44:48,270 --> 00:44:49,520
What if I already went home?

815
00:44:50,960 --> 00:44:53,040
There was only one session of
'Doraemon the Movie' today.

816
00:44:53,350 --> 00:44:55,250
So I estimated when it would end.

817
00:44:56,210 --> 00:44:57,280
You knew, huh?

818
00:44:58,760 --> 00:44:59,440
And what about that guy...

819
00:45:02,160 --> 00:45:03,480
What about Mon?

820
00:45:03,740 --> 00:45:05,360
Why did he keep you waiting all by yourself?

821
00:45:05,520 --> 00:45:07,960
If it was me, I wouldn't do that.

822
00:45:08,450 --> 00:45:10,230
I told him to go.

823
00:45:11,150 --> 00:45:12,920
He always does whatever I say.

824
00:45:13,550 --> 00:45:14,720
Yeah, but still.

825
00:45:14,940 --> 00:45:16,070
Next time,

826
00:45:16,090 --> 00:45:17,480
if you're not going to call,

827
00:45:17,620 --> 00:45:18,920
at least leave me a text.

828
00:45:19,160 --> 00:45:20,440
I worried about you, alright?

829
00:45:20,770 --> 00:45:22,070
What if there was an accident

830
00:45:22,090 --> 00:45:23,520
and I had to skip the film,

831
00:45:23,560 --> 00:45:24,520
what would you do?

832
00:45:24,540 --> 00:45:26,050
Would you just wait there until tomorrow?

833
00:45:27,980 --> 00:45:29,240
You're still acting nonchalant?

834
00:45:29,330 --> 00:45:31,150
Are you even listening?

835
00:45:31,170 --> 00:45:32,430
I'm worried about you, okay?

836
00:45:33,760 --> 00:45:34,640
Mm.

837
00:45:37,240 --> 00:45:37,920
- Huh?
- Give me that if you won't eat.

838
00:45:37,940 --> 00:45:39,540
Hey, Jane. Please, no!

839
00:45:40,260 --> 00:45:41,640
Give it back.

840
00:45:43,890 --> 00:45:45,290
- I want to try...
- No, I'm about to...

841
00:45:46,090 --> 00:45:46,880
Hey, Jane!

842
00:45:47,060 --> 00:45:48,060
Jane!!

843
00:45:49,660 --> 00:45:51,040
Have you tried slurping it like this?

844
00:45:51,060 --> 00:45:52,170
This is how it's done.

845
00:46:17,160 --> 00:46:17,980
Jane, let's go.

846
00:46:18,000 --> 00:46:19,850
You should head back. I'll call you a ride.

847
00:46:20,350 --> 00:46:21,350
Uh, Jaab...

848
00:46:22,040 --> 00:46:23,340
We'll...

849
00:46:25,170 --> 00:46:26,760
use my phone, okay?

850
00:46:28,750 --> 00:46:29,510
Uh...

851
00:46:29,530 --> 00:46:31,200
Yeah, sure.

852
00:46:56,540 --> 00:46:57,340
Jane.

853
00:46:57,640 --> 00:46:58,760
Did we pin the wrong location?

854
00:46:59,460 --> 00:47:00,360
I'm sorry.

855
00:47:00,390 --> 00:47:01,670
I was busy with my phone.

856
00:47:01,690 --> 00:47:03,120
I didn't notice where we were heading.

857
00:47:05,720 --> 00:47:06,550
How about this?

858
00:47:06,680 --> 00:47:08,140
Wait here.

859
00:47:08,160 --> 00:47:09,930
I'll get the key for Thua-Dam.

860
00:47:09,950 --> 00:47:11,050
I'll drive you home.

861
00:47:11,760 --> 00:47:12,520
Jaab.

862
00:47:12,810 --> 00:47:13,360
Huh?

863
00:47:16,360 --> 00:47:18,200
Is the view from the rooftop at night here...

864
00:47:18,950 --> 00:47:20,040
beautiful?

865
00:47:20,860 --> 00:47:21,560
Huh?!

866
00:47:24,560 --> 00:47:25,760
Can I...

867
00:47:26,150 --> 00:47:28,920
Can I go up there and check it out?

868
00:47:55,460 --> 00:47:56,350
Jane,

869
00:47:56,960 --> 00:47:58,040
is something wrong?

870
00:48:02,920 --> 00:48:04,880
I should be asking you that, Jaab.

871
00:48:07,640 --> 00:48:08,560
Well...

872
00:48:08,580 --> 00:48:09,960
I'm fine, Jane.

873
00:48:10,270 --> 00:48:11,440
Totally fine.

874
00:48:18,750 --> 00:48:22,000
I'm sorry for taking up your time
so late at night.

875
00:48:24,360 --> 00:48:25,840
I...

876
00:48:27,270 --> 00:48:29,560
I've been mustering up
the courage all day,

877
00:48:32,760 --> 00:48:34,700
but I could only manage to tell you just now.

878
00:48:39,540 --> 00:48:41,520
My world is small, Jaab.

879
00:48:42,860 --> 00:48:45,050
I never had to guess how people would feel.

880
00:48:45,850 --> 00:48:47,840
To be honest, I don't even know how to do that.

881
00:48:52,960 --> 00:48:54,760
But I want to care about how you feel.

882
00:48:57,850 --> 00:48:58,800
Jane?

883
00:49:00,020 --> 00:49:02,080
I have only a few people in my life,

884
00:49:10,150 --> 00:49:12,400
probably even less than
the petals of these flowers here.

885
00:49:16,050 --> 00:49:18,000
I know for sure that
there's something up with you.

886
00:49:19,750 --> 00:49:21,360
But I can't tell exactly what it is.

887
00:49:29,860 --> 00:49:32,000
Something's been bothering me.

888
00:49:33,150 --> 00:49:34,550
Recently, I mean.

889
00:49:35,770 --> 00:49:37,000
I'm sorry for worrying you,

890
00:49:37,020 --> 00:49:37,720
but...

891
00:49:38,360 --> 00:49:39,120
it...

892
00:49:39,750 --> 00:49:41,650
it has nothing to do with you at all, Jane.

893
00:49:41,670 --> 00:49:43,000
Don't think too much about it.

894
00:49:46,540 --> 00:49:49,120
Before I could have the courage
to ask someone to come over,

895
00:49:53,260 --> 00:49:55,950
before I could sit in their car for hours

896
00:49:55,970 --> 00:49:58,250
without feeling uncomfortable,

897
00:50:02,160 --> 00:50:03,520
before I could...

898
00:50:04,560 --> 00:50:06,840
share some fruits with them

899
00:50:08,150 --> 00:50:10,550
without worrying
whether they'd like them or not,

900
00:50:16,140 --> 00:50:17,280
and before I could...

901
00:50:19,450 --> 00:50:21,360
call somebody "a friend,"

902
00:50:23,400 --> 00:50:25,000
it's really hard for me, Jaab.

903
00:50:26,350 --> 00:50:28,160
I'm just worried

904
00:50:28,450 --> 00:50:29,720
to see you like this.

905
00:50:31,000 --> 00:50:32,800
And I don't want to lose you.

906
00:50:38,550 --> 00:50:39,280
Then...

907
00:50:40,350 --> 00:50:41,800
give me some time.

908
00:50:42,350 --> 00:50:45,080
I promise you that
everything will be back to normal.

909
00:50:47,840 --> 00:50:49,800
What do you mean?

910
00:50:51,650 --> 00:50:53,280
What exactly is normal, Jaab?

911
00:50:57,860 --> 00:50:59,000
Is it like...

912
00:50:59,850 --> 00:51:01,040
how everything used to be?

913
00:51:02,840 --> 00:51:03,960
Or is it like...

914
00:51:05,460 --> 00:51:07,080
back before you knew that

915
00:51:07,750 --> 00:51:09,040
I've been talking to Mon?

916
00:51:48,520 --> 00:51:51,200
[Don't you like what's going on
between Mon and me?]

917
00:52:08,000 --> 00:52:12,160
[Are you having a crush on me, Jaab?]

918
00:52:23,620 --> 00:52:27,640
[I'm sorry]

919
00:52:29,860 --> 00:52:30,440
Jane...

920
00:52:30,750 --> 00:52:31,840
Jane, Jane, Jane.

921
00:52:31,860 --> 00:52:32,880
Jane, Jane, Jane.

922
00:52:33,400 --> 00:52:34,600
Jane, Jane, Jane.

923
00:52:34,620 --> 00:52:35,450
Jane...

924
00:52:35,470 --> 00:52:36,000
Jane...

925
00:52:43,770 --> 00:52:44,490
Jane.

926
00:52:44,510 --> 00:52:45,140
Please...

927
00:52:45,160 --> 00:52:47,080
Look at me.

928
00:52:47,310 --> 00:52:48,130
Jane.

929
00:52:48,470 --> 00:52:50,480
You didn't do anything wrong.

930
00:52:51,450 --> 00:52:53,260
None of this is your fault.

931
00:52:53,560 --> 00:52:54,650
Do you understand?

932
00:52:58,820 --> 00:52:59,840
Did I...

933
00:53:00,060 --> 00:53:02,480
hurt your feelings without realizing it?

934
00:53:12,080 --> 00:53:13,480
Getting to know you

935
00:53:14,720 --> 00:53:16,960
is the most valuable thing
that has ever happened to me,

936
00:53:17,260 --> 00:53:17,920
so...

937
00:53:18,460 --> 00:53:20,420
how could you ever hurt me?

938
00:53:23,480 --> 00:53:27,280
You're one of the valuable things
in my life, too.

939
00:53:27,890 --> 00:53:29,920
I just don't want to lose you

940
00:53:30,910 --> 00:53:32,750
because of what I didn't realize.

941
00:53:33,660 --> 00:53:34,520
Mm.

942
00:53:35,760 --> 00:53:36,720
I won't...

943
00:53:36,970 --> 00:53:38,760
disappear from your life that easily either.

944
00:53:39,360 --> 00:53:40,530
I won't leave even if you tell me to.

945
00:53:40,550 --> 00:53:41,640
Okay?

946
00:53:42,940 --> 00:53:43,780
You promise?

947
00:53:44,740 --> 00:53:45,640
Of course.

948
00:53:47,550 --> 00:53:49,070
Just your pinky promise

949
00:53:50,700 --> 00:53:52,050
is enough to make me smile.

950
00:53:54,320 --> 00:53:56,430
A friend who's so easy to tease

951
00:53:56,450 --> 00:53:57,840
and who's this sweet,

952
00:53:57,940 --> 00:53:59,450
who could ever let you go so easily?

953
00:53:59,840 --> 00:54:00,520
Hm?

954
00:54:04,460 --> 00:54:06,160
If you don't believe me, try it.

955
00:54:20,060 --> 00:54:20,920
See?

956
00:54:21,440 --> 00:54:22,280
Just this

957
00:54:22,750 --> 00:54:24,720
is enough to put a smile on my face, Jane.

958
00:54:29,400 --> 00:54:30,760
I promise you

959
00:54:31,720 --> 00:54:33,060
that everything between us

960
00:54:33,080 --> 00:54:34,440
will go back to normal.

961
00:54:36,360 --> 00:54:37,850
And what about your feelings?

962
00:54:43,460 --> 00:54:44,760
Come on, Jane...

963
00:54:50,060 --> 00:54:50,800
Yeah.

964
00:54:53,050 --> 00:54:55,360
If anything were to be
in the wrong place right now,

965
00:54:55,950 --> 00:54:57,240
there would be only one thing,

966
00:54:57,850 --> 00:55:00,460
and that would be the way I feel.

967
00:55:00,650 --> 00:55:02,160
I crossed the line.

968
00:55:03,640 --> 00:55:04,640
So please,

969
00:55:05,860 --> 00:55:07,400
give me some time, Jane.

970
00:55:10,120 --> 00:55:10,840
And...

971
00:55:12,550 --> 00:55:15,340
I promise you, I'll step back.

972
00:55:41,650 --> 00:55:42,960
Come on, Jane.

973
00:55:43,050 --> 00:55:43,770
Let me see it.

974
00:55:43,790 --> 00:55:45,880
Let me see the kisses from an angel.

975
00:55:45,950 --> 00:55:46,950
Let me see one here.

976
00:55:53,480 --> 00:55:55,000
Well done.

977
00:55:55,020 --> 00:55:56,360
You always do whatever I say.

978
00:55:57,340 --> 00:55:58,720
You're adorable, Jane.

979
00:56:08,180 --> 00:56:10,240
All the feelings inside me are tangled up,

980
00:56:11,970 --> 00:56:14,520
both the best and the worst ones.

981
00:56:14,860 --> 00:56:16,320
I can't tell at all...

982
00:56:16,760 --> 00:56:18,920
whether I'm actually happy or not.

983
00:56:37,380 --> 00:56:38,770
Jaab said

984
00:56:39,050 --> 00:56:41,050
he needed time for everything to go back to normal.

985
00:56:41,920 --> 00:56:43,680
You'll actually pull through, right?

986
00:56:44,090 --> 00:56:45,400
He already has Mon.

987
00:56:45,570 --> 00:56:47,480
If I stole Jane from him,
then I'd be nothing but a bastard.

988
00:56:48,330 --> 00:56:52,010
Are you sad because Jaab has a crush on you,

989
00:56:52,030 --> 00:56:53,360
or are you sad because

990
00:56:53,680 --> 00:56:55,480
he's giving up on you?

991
00:56:56,000 --> 00:56:57,360
If it was you,

992
00:56:57,870 --> 00:56:59,800
would you go back in time and change it?
